{"comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAABQ_qc9w","author":{"login":"hachej"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Owner review card — PR #1424 (fixes #1391)\n\n**Presentation artifact:** `.handoff/pr-1424-presentation.html` (generated locally in the `.worktrees/fix-1391` lane worktree via `scripts/present-pr.mjs`; not committed — `.handoff/` is gitignored by repo convention). `exec_ui`/`ask_user` panes aren't available in this environment, so posting the review card here instead.\n\n**Scope:** Escape did not close open dropdown menus in real browsers — the shared `useKeyboardShortcuts` Escape handler only dismissed modals/panels. Adds a dropdown-close branch to that handler, wires it through `ChatLayout`, and adds a real-browser Playwright spec (`apps/workspace-playground/e2e/dropdown-escape.spec.ts`) proving Escape closes the menu end-to-end — the class of bug a jsdom-based unit test alone would not catch. Modal/panel Escape behavior is untouched.\n\n**Proof:** CI is fully green on the functional path — Lint, Typecheck, Unit Tests, Unit Tests Changed, E2E, Invariants, Bundle Budget all pass on head sha `e88f639`. `UI Review` fails, but on `workspace-command-palette` mobile hard gates unrelated to dropdowns/Escape — the same fixture fails with different violation IDs on PR #1423, which touches a completely different file, so this looks like a pre-existing/flaky gate on that fixture rather than something this PR introduced.\n\n**Residuals:** UI Review failure not root-caused beyond \"different unrelated PR trips the same gate\" — flagging for owner triage. No deep/thermo review recorded yet on this PR (recorded as `NOT RECORDED` in the artifact).\n\n**Validate locally:**\n```\ncd .worktrees/fix-1391\npnpm -C packages/workspace test -- useKeyboardShortcuts\npnpm -C apps/workspace-playground exec playwright test e2e/dropdown-escape.spec.ts\n```\nClick path: open the workspace-playground app, open any dropdown/select menu in the chat layout chrome, press Escape, confirm