{"comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAABQ_qXWg","author":{"login":"hachej"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Owner review card — PR #1423 (fixes #1392)\n\n**Presentation artifact:** `.handoff/pr-1423-presentation.html` (generated locally in the `.worktrees/fix-1392` lane worktree via `scripts/present-pr.mjs`; not committed — `.handoff/` is gitignored by repo convention). `exec_ui`/`ask_user` panes aren't available in this environment, so posting the review card here instead.\n\n**Scope:** `shadow-md` rendered opaque instead of transparent-tinted in both themes. One-line fix in `packages/ui/src/styles.css` so its shadow color resolves through the same theme-contract token path as `shadow-sm`/`shadow-lg`, plus a `theme-css-contract.test.ts` assertion locking it in. No component/layout/JS changes.\n\n**Proof:** New/updated contract test passes locally; CI is red but on unrelated jobs:\n- `Unit Tests` / `Unit Tests Changed` fail on `packages/agent/.../lifecycle.test.ts` — a timing assertion (`expected 265 to be less than 250`) in a package this PR does not touch. Looks like a flaky threshold, not a regression from this diff.\n- `UI Review` fails on `workspace-command-palette` mobile hard gates — the same fixture surface fails with *different* violation IDs on PR #1424 too, pointing to a pre-existing/flaky hard gate unrelated to this CSS change.\n\nNeither failure touches `packages/ui/src/styles.css` or the theme contract test.\n\n**Residuals:** CI failures above are unexplained beyond \"doesn't touch this PR's diff\" — flagging for owner triage rather than asserting flaky with certainty. No deep/thermo review has been run on this PR yet (recorded as `NOT RECORDED` in the artifact).\n\n**Validate locally:**\n```\ncd .worktrees/fix-1392\npnpm -C packages/ui test        # or: pnpm -C packages/workspace test -- theme-css-contract\n```\nVisual check: open any surface using `shadow-md` (e.g. a dropdown/menu panel) in both light and dark theme and confirm the shadow reads as a soft transparent tint, not an opaque box.\n","createdAt":"2026-08-27T06:56:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/pull/1423#issuecomment-5435463514","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAABQ_rsbQ","author":{"login":"hachej"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Thermo review gate — REVISE\n\n**Reviewer:** Sol medium / T2 thermo  \n**Target:** `cdd8cd56005fc93c32417f05f5b86bebc94d51a6`\n\n### Findings, highest severity first\n\n1. **HIGH — this patch does not change the generated `.shadow-md` runtime rule.** I compiled both `HEAD^` and this head from `packages/ui/src/styles.css` with the checked-in PostCSS/Tailwind pipeline. Both outputs contain the same `.shadow-md` declaration:\n   `--tw-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px var(--tw-shadow-color, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1)), 0 2px 4px -2px var(--tw-shadow-color, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1))`\n   followed by the same `box-shadow`. The added `--shadow-md` source declaration is consumed during generation and does not survive into the built CSS as a variable declaration. Therefore the reported computed-style failure cannot be fixed by this diff as written. Please reproduce the actual served/consumer failure and make the generated or served CSS materially differ on that path.\n\n2. **HIGH — the new assertion is source-shape coverage, not a regression test for #1392.** It passes because a nonzero token was typed into `@theme`, even though the before/after generated utility is identical. This is a weakened proof boundary: it cannot fail on the actual transparent computed shadow. Add a build/consumer-level assertion over the emitted rule or, preferably, a browser computed-style regression that fails on the parent and passes on the fix.\n\n### Verification boundary\n\n**Verified:** fetched PR diff and issue #1392; inspected the source and test; ran workspace `theme-css-contract.test.ts` (3/3) and UI tests (7/7); independently compiled parent and head with `@tailwindcss/postcss` 4.3.3 and compared the emitted `.shadow-md` rule; confirmed the PR head remained unchanged before review.\n\n**Taken on trust / not verified:** the original console-spike browser observation and claimed consumer build reproduction were not available as runnable evidence here. Current CI also has unrelated/red jobs, so I did not treat CI status as proof of this fix.","createdAt":"2026-08-27T06:59:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/pull/1423#issuecomment-5435485293","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"headRefOid":"cdd8cd56005fc93c32417f05f5b86bebc94d51a6","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T06:02:54Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/actions/runs/33044464778/job/98425153770","name":"Detect Changes","startedAt":"2026-08-27T06:02:42Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T06:02:51Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/actions/runs/33044464752/job/98425153577","name":"Action Pins","startedAt":"2026-08-27T06:02:42Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Workflow Invariants"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T06:02:49Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/actions/runs/33044464778/job/98425153742","name":"Action Pins","startedAt":"2026-08-27T06:02:42Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T06:04:54Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/actions/runs/33044464752/job/98425153415","name":"Runtime Refactor P8","startedAt":"2026-08-27T06:02:42Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Workflow Invariants"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T06:02:53Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/actions/runs