The first exact end-to-end run did not pass, so I’m stopping the shipping path as requested instead of turning a deterministic product defect into an exemption. The settled hard gates identify the same root control in every failed mobile/tablet state: `Archived0`, measured at ~20px high against the existing 44px coarse-pointer contract. This also matches both unrelated CI artifacts; their changing IDs were screenshot-derived state IDs, while the underlying violation was identical. I’m collecting the final source-level evidence for both signatures now; there will be no commit, push, or PR unless the 5/5 gate is achievable without weakening coverage.
