I did not ship a partial fix. The required 5/5 gate is currently impossible without changing app code or weakening a valid hard gate.

Root causes:

- Mobile/tablet failures are not screenshot/font/hash nondeterminism. PRs #1423/#1424 had byte-identical known screenshots. The changing IDs are screenshot-derived state IDs.
- Every underlying failure is the same newly introduced app control: `Archived0`, approximately `20px` high on coarse-pointer viewports versus the existing `44px` requirement. It was introduced by archive-sessions commit `ca9cd66c6e`; no coarse-pointer sizing rule covers it.
- Bombadil additionally modeled a 390px fine-pointer browser as touch. The prototype separates compact layout from coarse-pointer behavior.
- The sidebar navigation can become terminal because agent discovery is a one-shot fetch: rejection stores an empty roster with no retry. The prototype reloads once instead of waiting indefinitely.

Proof:

- Harness unit tests: `94/94` passed.
- Harness typecheck: passed.
- First exact sidebar review run: failed, so the consecutive 5/5 sequence was stopped immediately.
- All 11 failed mobile/tablet states reported only `agent-touch-targets`, with `Archived0` at `19.7px`. Evidence: [hard-gates.json](/tmp/ui-review-1390-baseline/hard-gates.json).

Uncommitted tools-only prototype changes include capture settling, readiness reload, pointer-model corrections, and tests under [tools/ui-review](/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/retest-1390/tools/ui-review). The unrelated `sol-1390.log` remains untouched.

No commit, push, or PR was created. PR URL: N/A. The app-level `Archived` disclosure must first either receive a 44px coarse-pointer target or stop rendering at zero archived chats; then #1390 can be rerun for the required 5/5 proof.
